<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ouedraogo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ouedraogo is the legendary founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mossi">Mossi</a> people of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burkina-faso">Burkina Faso</a>. Tradition tells that he was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yennenga">Yennenga</a>, a warrior princess of Mamprugu who rode north on a stallion, and of a hunter named Riale. His descendants are said to have founded the Mossi kingdoms, including Tenkodogo and Ouagadougou, and his name, meaning stallion, is a common surname in Burkina Faso.</p></div>
